behaviour: '**REFACTOR-024 SQL-LAYER + SERVICE-LAYER REGRESSION TEST.** `listAllWithStatusOpen`
  has NO owner predicate — every authenticated caller of `GET /api/alerts` reads the entire
  platform''s open-alert stream. Confirmed at the canonical SQL primary source: lines
  143-145 `selectFrom(ALERT).where(ALERT.STATUS.eq(AlertStatusEnum.OPEN.getCode()))`
  with no JOIN on OWNERSHIP, no per-principal predicate. The outer-select pagination
  wrapper adds joins but no owner predicate. No test asserts the current cross-owner
  behaviour. A future security tightening that adds an owner predicate would silently
  change behaviour; an accidental owner-predicate regression would silently change
  behaviour. Pin the current behaviour to make the change deliberate. test_class:
  integration / security. STRENGTHENED batch S — the AlertServiceImpl service-tier
  closure sidecar (2026-05-20) PRIMARY-SOURCE confirms `listAll` (lines 76-80) is
  a three-line pass-through to `listAllWithStatusOpen` with no owner filter, no role
  check, no permission gate. The service IS THE MISSING-DEFENCE LAYER (not just the
  repository per batch H). The compound surface now has THREE corroborating tiers:
  controller (batch A — AlertController.getAllAlerts, severity HIGH), service (batch
  S — AlertServiceImpl.listAll, three-line pass-through), repository (batch H — ReactiveAlertRepositoryImpl.listAllWithStatusOpen,
  SQL primary source). The full forge-and-display compound for F-007 + REFACTOR-024
  is now fully traced.'
